{
  "chapter": "patterns/security/untrusted-content-marking",
  "tier": "micro",
  "notes": [
    "Trust is a property of provenance, not of content. Marking happens at ingestion,",
    "travels with the chunk, and the ceiling of a context is the lowest trust in it.",
    "Order: system > reviewed > external. A context is only as trusted as its worst source."
  ],
  "order": ["external", "reviewed", "system"],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "an-empty-context-is-fully-trusted",
      "sources": [],
      "ceiling": "system"
    },
    {
      "id": "a-single-reviewed-source-caps-at-reviewed",
      "sources": ["reviewed"],
      "ceiling": "reviewed"
    },
    {
      "id": "one-external-source-drags-the-whole-context-down",
      "sources": ["system", "reviewed", "external"],
      "ceiling": "external"
    },
    {
      "id": "position-does-not-matter",
      "sources": ["external", "system", "system"],
      "ceiling": "external"
    },
    {
      "id": "quantity-does-not-matter",
      "sources": ["system", "system", "system", "external"],
      "ceiling": "external"
    },
    {
      "id": "all-system-sources-stay-at-system",
      "sources": ["system", "system"],
      "ceiling": "system"
    },
    {
      "id": "an-unknown-marking-is-treated-as-external",
      "sources": ["system", "scraped-from-somewhere"],
      "ceiling": "external"
    }
  ]
}
